{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1790273766325086307,"compiled_state":{"alias":"diet-capsizable-sparrow","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"8ad5ab328ecf2eb0e7fe00e16a3026ba86b469e3a99fd73d4c2036eb82bbf3af","event_uuid":"aa2f19f6-20f2-4d4e-ac65-49ffbd3bae64","position":{"commit_sha":"0886e70daf58a8c82551d44e1f636677f201351d","position":"1790270993411121757-aa2f19f6-20f2-4d4e-ac65-49ffbd3bae64"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"277b633724832c6633cd747d9ec340fbec3c7020a29d6215ff94f4a54f90fcd5","event_uuid":"139ecc80-e8c3-40ff-9ab0-d2a836bcc220","position":{"commit_sha":"992b97c3ef92021a105b71339a4e18ce46da9033","position":"1790271034859536124-139ecc80-e8c3-40ff-9ab0-d2a836bcc220"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"245a804fdd1275d81e4bf10b76fe016a2229271a36fa6be965aa9e23be662b19","event_uuid":"d5e10748-cb22-45c5-8ff6-328908dd4aee","position":{"commit_sha":"986fe68653b7fa52bc566c28cdbeed9e0a92d154","position":"1790271047594135874-d5e10748-cb22-45c5-8ff6-328908dd4aee"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"17df2c30327909281b88bbb2acfb43bda2a9f8ba89c9af0f57aa8b509318a4e9","event_uuid":"53a9f55d-d639-4425-9adb-d882466273f0","position":{"commit_sha":"790fa7903eb87d70fb100cb10a3c89f1ac26a789","position":"1790271063444865188-53a9f55d-d639-4425-9adb-d882466273f0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1790270993411121757,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d5e10748-cb22-45c5-8ff6-328908dd4aee","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3083-ada3-3a0f-4051"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` converts CloudWatch token counts\ninto dollars via a rate table derived daily from Cost Explorer and matched to\nmodels by string heuristics. That layer produced four distinct defects in the\ntwelve days since the cap was deployed (2026-09-12):\n\n1. `_rate_for`/`_match` direction-suffix collision: the candidate suffix\n   `input-token-count` also matches the key `...-cache-write-input-token-count`\n   and the longest match wins, so a model's input rate resolves to its cache-write\n   rate. Fires iff the ModelId has no version suffix — live for\n   `claude-sonnet-4-6`, `claude-opus-4-7`, `claude-opus-4-8`, `claude-opus-5`.\n2. `_normalise` mismatch: label `Nova2.0Lite` gives `nova20lite`, model id\n   `us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0` gives `nova2litev10`. Neither contains the other,\n   so an existing correct rate is missed and the model falls to\n   `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K`, set far above any real rate.\n3. `BEDROCK_SERVICE_VALUES`, the hardcoded CE service allowlist introduced by\n   3083-ada3-3a0f-4051, omits `Claude Opus 4.8`, `Claude Opus 5`,\n   `Claude Opus 4.5`, `Cohere Rerank v3.5` and `Claude 3 Haiku`, so the\n   authoritative CE signal sees about a third of real Bedrock spend.\n4. `MARKETPLACE_TOKEN_SUFFIXES` handles only CamelCase usage types. AWS bills\n   newer marketplace models in snake_case (`USE1_input_tokens_standard-Units`)\n   and publishes `_Global` variants; `_refresh_rates` silently skips both.\n\nTwo reached production unalarmed: one model was priced at the fail-closed\nfallback rate for seven days, emitting 6,112 `fail-closed fallback` log events\nwhile the cap's estimate ran at roughly twice settled billing; and the\nmarketplace-units defect fixed by Gerrit 3032 had the estimate five orders of\nmagnitude above reality.\n\nThese are one class, not four bugs: matching model identifiers against billing\nlabels with substring and suffix heuristics. Four shapes of that mismatch have\nalready occurred, so the class will recur.\n\n## Approach\n\nDelete the pricing-derivation layer; price every token at a ceiling rate for its\ndirection, set above the highest per-direction rate observed on this account, so\nthe estimate is an upper bound and the cap cannot fire late. Per UTC day:\n\n    spend = max( sum over regions and the four token metrics of\n                   undimensioned CloudWatch Sum * CEILING[metric],\n                 ce_spend )\n\nCost Explorer stays in the enforcement expression: it is the only signal covering\nBedrock spend that publishes no token metric (Cohere Rerank is live; provisioned\nthroughput, batch and customization are structural), and it is orthogonal to\nevery defect above.\n\nCloudWatch reads move from per-ModelId enumeration to the four undimensioned\naggregates. Verified equivalent over 2026-09-14 to 09-24: the aggregate and the\nsum of per-ModelId series agree to four decimal places, the aggregate being very\nslightly larger because `list_metrics` returns only recently-active series.\n\n### Accepted limitation\n\nPricing at the ceiling over-estimates for models much cheaper than the priciest.\nOn this account the cheapest are two orders of magnitude below it, and two models\ncurrently bill nothing for cache-write, making the factor unbounded. A large\nembedding or small-model batch job can therefore trip the cap at a small fraction\nof intended spend. Accepted deliberately for simplicity; must be stated in the\nREADME. The remedy if it bites is an exact-match `{ModelId: rate}` override table\ndefaulting to the ceiling — exact equality only, never substring or normalisation\nmatching, so it cannot reopen this class.\n\n## Figures\n\nMachine-local policy bars spend totals, unit costs, budgets, cap thresholds and\nbill figures from the tracker, because the tickets branch auto-pushes to the\npublic GitHub mirror. The ceiling constants, threshold, observed rate table,\n50-day back-test distribution and incident figures are in the operator's\nlocal-only note `~/Desktop/bedrock-cap-redesign-local-only/design.md`. Implement\nfrom that file. Copy no figure from it into this ticket, a comment, a session\nlog, a commit message or the README.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. The enforcement expression contains no model-identifier matching and no\n   usage-type parsing. `_refresh_rates`, `_rate_for`, `_seed_for`, `_normalise`,\n   `_strip_billing_region`, `_marketplace_rate_key` and `_rate_key_for_ce_group`\n   are deleted, along with `SEED_RATES`, `RATE_OVERRIDES`,\n   `BEDROCK_SERVICE_VALUES`, `MARKETPLACE_TOKEN_SUFFIXES`, `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K`,\n   `MARKETPLACE_TOKENS_PER_RATE_UNIT` and the `TOKEN_METRICS` multipliers. A test\n   asserts none of those names survives in the module.\n2. `_metered_spend` issues exactly four undimensioned `GetMetricData` queries per\n   configured region and performs no `list_metrics` call on the enforcement path.\n3. A `CEILING` mapping supplies one rate per token metric from the local-only\n   note. A test asserts each value is at least the highest rate for that direction\n   in a recorded Cost Explorer payload fixture.\n4. Enforcement still compares `max(ceiling_estimate, ce_spend)` against the\n   threshold. `_ce_spend_today` classifies Bedrock spend by predicate — service\n   equals `Amazon Bedrock` or ends with the Bedrock Edition suffix — not by an\n   enumerated allowlist. A test proves the predicate matches every Bedrock service\n   in the recorded payload, including the five the allowlist omitted.\n5. The cap does not release on a tick where every CloudWatch query returned no\n   datapoints; releasing requires a positive, non-empty reading below threshold. A\n   test covers the empty read and asserts the deny stays attached.\n6. Threshold and warning values in `infra/terraform/bedrock_spend_cap.tf` are set\n   to the design note's values, chosen so the median effective cap lands near the\n   intended daily figure.\n7. `state[\"rates\"]`, `state[\"rates_day\"]` and `metered_estimated` are removed from\n   the state document and the handler's return value, with `MeteredRate` and the\n   `\" (estimated)\"` rendering. A test asserts the persisted state carries no rate\n   table.\n8. A daily guard compares the ceiling estimate for a settled day against Cost\n   Explorer for that day and emits an SNS warning if the estimate is below actual,\n   i.e. the upper-bound invariant is violated. The guard cannot attach or detach\n   the deny policy.\n9. A daily `list_metrics` ModelId diff emits an SNS warning when a ModelId appears\n   that is not in a recorded known set, surfacing a new model on first use rather\n   than after it is billed.\n10. On the warn and trip paths only, per-model token counts are logged for\n    attribution. No prices, no matching.\n11. Tests are driven by recorded real Cost Explorer and `list_metrics` payloads\n    checked into the repository, not synthesized fixtures. The recorded CE payload\n    contains CamelCase, snake_case, `_Global` and a non-token usage type in one\n    file. A property test asserts every ModelId in the recorded `list_metrics`\n    payload is priced by the ceiling with no fallback path.\n12. The README documents the accepted over-estimate, the resulting effective-cap\n    band qualitatively, and that the figure is an upper bound rather than an\n    estimate of actual spend.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nOptimistic concurrency on the SSM state write, and the `signal_unavailable`\nrelease deadlock: fourteen days of logs show zero occurrences of either against\nroughly seven thousand pricing failures.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py","reason":"Delete the pricing-derivation layer and the seven named functions; replace _metered_spend with undimensioned aggregates priced at CEILING; keep max(ceiling, ce); add the empty-read release guard, the daily invariant guard and the ModelId diff"},{"path":"infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/README.md","reason":"Document the upper-bound semantics, the accepted cheap-model over-estimate and the effective-cap band"},{"path":"infra/terraform/bedrock_spend_cap.tf","reason":"Set threshold and warning values per the local-only design note"},{"path":"tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py","reason":"Rewrite around recorded payloads; assert deleted names are absent, ceiling covers observed rates, predicate matches every Bedrock service, empty read does not release, state carries no rate table"},{"path":"tests/infra/fixtures/bedrock_ce_payload.json","reason":"New recorded Cost Explorer payload containing CamelCase, snake_case, _Global and a non-token usage type"},{"path":"tests/infra/fixtures/bedrock_list_metrics.json","reason":"New recorded list_metrics payload covering every live ModelId and the non-token SearchUnits metric"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","3083-ada3-3a0f-4051"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["bedrock","cost","infra","simplification"],"ticket_id":"7775-46e5-3fd7-42d2","ticket_type":"story","title":"Replace the Bedrock spend cap's per-model pricing layer with a ceiling rate per token direction","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["aa2f19f6-20f2-4d4e-ac65-49ffbd3bae64","139ecc80-e8c3-40ff-9ab0-d2a836bcc220","d5e10748-cb22-45c5-8ff6-328908dd4aee","53a9f55d-d639-4425-9adb-d882466273f0"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1790273766325086307,"uuid":"e7144b79-efc3-4e49-8191-06d4e1033f53"}